WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.685 --> 00:00:14.266
Jason couldn't concentrate.

2
00:00:15.186 --> 00:00:16.326
He couldn't even walk.

3
00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:18.908
His legs were so itchy!

4
00:00:20.208 --> 00:00:23.170
Last night he and his dad had eaten dinner outside.

5
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.312
By the time they went inside, Jason was covered in mosquito bites.

6
00:00:29.936 --> 00:00:32.038
Itchy, horrible mosquito bites.

7
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.601
"I can't take it anymore!"

8
00:00:36.742 --> 00:00:39.384
Jason showed everyone the red spots on his legs.

9
00:00:39.404 --> 00:00:42.447
"Wow," said Nina.

10
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.348
"They look itchy."

11
00:00:44.368 --> 00:00:48.572
"You should have used bug spray," said Izzie.

12
00:00:48.592 --> 00:00:52.935
"I can't use bug spray," Jason said.

13
00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:54.457
"Why not?"

14
00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:55.678
Nina asked.

15
00:00:56.578 --> 00:00:58.160
"Because I'm allergic to the chemicals."

16
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.040
Jason frowned.

17
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.121
"Well then it's your lucky day!"

18
00:01:03.661 --> 00:01:04.301
said Mr.

19
00:01:04.362 --> 00:01:06.602
Dunn. "Lucky?"

20
00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:07.882
Jason echoed.

21
00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:10.863
"What's lucky about mosquito bites?"

22
00:01:12.064 --> 00:01:15.244
"We're making Campers' Bug Spray today," Mr.

23
00:01:15.304 --> 00:01:16.145
Dunn explained.

24
00:01:16.165 --> 00:01:19.146
"It's all-natural bug spray."

25
00:01:20.326 --> 00:01:22.306
"Really?" Jason didn't believe it.

26
00:01:22.326 --> 00:01:24.027
"How do you make it?"

27
00:01:24.047 --> 00:01:27.808
"Mr. Dunn is a chemistry teacher.

28
00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:30.650
So he can explain what to do.

29
00:01:31.631 --> 00:01:32.311
Right, Mr.

30
00:01:32.371 --> 00:01:35.574
Dunn?" Bobby looked at his teacher.

31
00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:37.395
"That's the plan."

32
00:01:37.755 --> 00:01:38.816
Mr. Dunn nodded.

33
00:01:38.836 --> 00:01:42.499
"Have a seat."

34
00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:53.028
some of these bottles are very strong oils called essential oils.

35
00:01:54.336 --> 00:02:00.700
By mixing certain essential oils, you can make a scent that will send mosquitoes running."

36
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.941
Mr. Dunn coughed.

37
00:02:04.502 --> 00:02:06.043
"I mean, flying."

38
00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:08.004
Nina giggled.

39
00:02:08.784 --> 00:02:09.585
She liked Mr.

40
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:10.685
Dunn's silly jokes.

41
00:02:10.705 --> 00:02:14.567
"But won't the scent make us want to run away too?"

42
00:02:14.988 --> 00:02:15.768
Ethan asked.

43
00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:17.789
"I don't think so.

44
00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.891
But you can decide for yourself in a minute," Mr.

45
00:02:21.931 --> 00:02:22.592
Dunn said.

46
00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:27.751
"Everyone, take one of the spray bottles and write your name on it.

47
00:02:28.972 --> 00:02:31.114
This will be your bug spray bottle."

48
00:02:34.977 --> 00:02:37.479
Jason carefully wrote his name on a bottle.

49
00:02:37.499 --> 00:02:43.884
"First we have to add what's called a base oil," said Mr.

50
00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:48.968
Dunn. "Today our base is olive oil.

51
00:02:50.084 --> 00:02:53.766
We'll start with that so the essential oils aren't so strong."

52
00:02:53.786 --> 00:02:56.548
"And so we won't be allergic?"

53
00:02:56.928 --> 00:02:57.908
Jason asked.

54
00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:04.772
"Yes. Some people get a rash from too much strong essential oil," Mr.

55
00:03:04.832 --> 00:03:05.493
Dunn said.

56
00:03:05.513 --> 00:03:09.455
"So we're going to carefully measure how much we put in."

57
00:03:10.916 --> 00:03:12.597
Everyone poured in the olive oil.

58
00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:17.119
Next Mr.

59
00:03:17.179 --> 00:03:18.360
Dunn held up a bottle.

60
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.161
"See this bottle's special top?

61
00:03:22.141 --> 00:03:26.763
The dropper helps us measure the eucalyptus oil one drop at a time."

62
00:03:27.784 --> 00:03:29.884
Mr. Dunn put a few drops in his hand.

63
00:03:31.425 --> 00:03:35.127
Then he rubbed his hands together and held them up for the kids to smell.

64
00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:39.909
"I like it," Izzie said.

65
00:03:39.929 --> 00:03:42.249
"It smells clean and fresh."

66
00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.510
Ethan took a sniff.

67
00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.072
"Wow! That's strong."

68
00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:52.198
"Put twenty drops into your bottle," Mr.

69
00:03:52.258 --> 00:03:52.939
Dunn said.

70
00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.501
Jason squinted.

71
00:03:55.521 --> 00:03:59.503
"I feel like it might sting my eyes," he said.

72
00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:02.305
"The oil could sting your eyes!"

73
00:04:02.746 --> 00:04:03.726
Mr. Dunn said.

74
00:04:03.746 --> 00:04:09.891
"So be very careful not to touch your eyes after handling essential oils."

75
00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:12.833
"What do we put in next?"

76
00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:14.054
Bobby asked.

77
00:04:15.114 --> 00:04:17.036
Mr. Dunn held up another bottle.

78
00:04:18.084 --> 00:04:19.685
"Citronella essential oil."

79
00:04:19.706 --> 00:04:24.529
"We have citronella candles in our backyard," Nina said.

80
00:04:24.549 --> 00:04:28.472
"Citronella keeps mosquitoes away," Mr.

81
00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:29.193
Dunn said.

82
00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:34.217
"So add twenty drops of this too.

83
00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:38.581
Shake it up and you're done!

84
00:04:39.842 --> 00:04:43.725
Next time we go on a hike, you can spray it on your arms and legs.

85
00:04:45.346 --> 00:04:47.708
Try this if you go outside tonight, Jason.

86
00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.522
I don't think any mosquitoes will bother you," Mr.

87
00:04:51.582 --> 00:04:52.202
Dunn said.

88
00:04:52.222 --> 00:04:55.484
"I'll try it," Jason said.

89
00:04:55.504 --> 00:05:00.107
"But after last night, I have no skin left to bite anyway!"
